The public interface (createChart, addSeries, timeScale, priceScale, panes, primitives, markers, names and default values of the
documented options) follows the Lightweight Charts v5 API for compatibility.

The geometry and behaviour parts (candle and bar widths, histogram columns, ticks, point markers, crosshair labels, last-bar rule,
choice of time labels, grid steps, scale widths) were rewritten by looking at the pixels produced by Lightweight Charts rather than by
copying its code, but a strict clean room is NOT claimed: the people who wrote them already knew the algorithms, and a second
independent review (see DERIVAZIONE.md) judged some of them derived. The function-by-function list is in DERIVAZIONE.md.

As requested by Lightweight Charts, whoever shows a chart built with this library must display, in a visible place (for example an
"About and credits" page), the attribution notice to TradingView with a link to https://www.tradingview.com/.

Lightweight Charts is a trademark of TradingView, Inc. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by TradingView, Inc.

The rest of the code (level of detail, data pyramid, WebGL drawing, script primitives, interaction) is original work by AnubiAI.
